---
title: Italian Sausage Sandwich
servings: 4
prepTime: 20 minutes
cookTime: 5 minutes
source: https://www.chelseasmessyapron.com/italian-sausage-hoagies/
tags: Pork
---

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a large #cast-iron pan{} over medium-high heat.
Add diced @bell peppers{2}(red or orange, finely chopped) and @yellow onion{1%cup}(diced); sauté for ~{5%minutes}.
Push veggies aside and increase heat to high.

Add @Italian sausage{16%oz}(ground or de-cased), plus a pinch of @salt and @pepper to the center of the pan.
Sear until browned, then crumble and cook until fully cooked and golden brown.

> Note: For a simpler sauce, purchase high quality ready-made marinara with garlic, basil, or other flavor profiles.
> Heat the sauce as instructed.

Reduce heat to medium-low.
Add @garlic{4%cloves}(minced), @dried oregano{1/2%tsp}, @garlic powder{1/2%tsp}, and @marinara sauce{2%cups}.
Cover and simmer for ~{5%minutes}.
Stir in the @fresh basil{1/3%cup}(thinly sliced).
Taste and adjust seasoning if needed.

Preheat oven to high broil, positioning the rack in the center.
Halve the @hoagie buns{}, spread the insides with @butter{}(softened), and lightly sprinkle with @garlic powder{1%tsp}.
Broil until lightly toasted ~{1%minute}. Remove from oven.

Set the top buns aside.
Divide the meat sauce evenly among the bottom buns.
Sprinkle @mozzarella cheese{8%ounces}(shredded) on top of the meat.
Broil until the cheese is melted ~{1%minute}.
Assemble the sandwiches and enjoy immediately to prevent them from getting soggy.

